From ed899d12ffb1b4082184b496a2934b6cd33751c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:19:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: move a route off a far pacing hold to an
 unheld class peer

2026-11-15 (hub core 992c0cb5e3b): openai-codex was pacing-held (limit 0)
until 11-20 22:40Z but never walled, so every default-routed card on the
fleet waited ~5 days while anthropic, the other deep-class provider, was
paced with free slots. resolve_dispatch_tier moved a route only off a wall,
and a pacing hold never records one.

Rule (hermes_cli/kanban_paced_reroute.py::paced_route), after the wall
reroutes: a default route, a review_unpinned reviewer, or a non-mandatory
concrete pin whose provider is stored `held` in llm_pacing.json with its
reset more than kanban.llm_pacing.reroute_after_s (default 3600) away, or
unknown, runs on the first eligible same-class peer (alternate_route /
independent reviewers / the pin's class peers) that is neither held nor
walled. tier_reason <reason>+paced:<provider>. A `paced` pool never moves a
route; mandatory pins, class selectors and require_model cards keep theirs;
no free peer keeps the base route. Reads only the stored pace (new
kanban_llm_pacing_dispatch.held_pools), no usage read. Queue notes and the
stall notice name the move ("next run rerouted: default+paced:openai-codex
-> anthropic/<model>").

kanban_pin_reroute: factor the class-peer pick into peer_route() so the pin
rule shares it.

Task: t_4cf6ea0228db1fb9
